/* `surface()` naming its catalog explicitly.

   This case used to name a catalog that does not exist — `.../other/catalog.json` —
   to prove the id on the `surface()` line beat the one passed to `compile()`.
   A2UI 1.0 refuses that outright:

     Unknown catalog 'https://travel-a2ui.dev/catalogs/other/catalog.json'.
     Available catalogs: ['https://travel-a2ui.dev/catalogs/a2ui-travel/catalog.json']

   and refuses the honest version of it too, because once a second catalog is
   loaded a surface may not name one at all:

     surface() names catalog '…/basic/catalog.json', but a surface names no
     catalog when several catalogs are active. Remove the catalog from the line
     and add catalogId only to components and function calls whose name several
     catalogs define.

   So 1.0 moved catalog selection off the surface and onto the components that
   need it. What is left to check here is that the name still reaches
   `createSurface` from this line, which is what the rest of the pipeline reads
   it from. */
surface("sidebar-filters", catalogId="https://travel-a2ui.dev/catalogs/a2ui-travel/catalog.json")
h = Text("Filters", variant="h3")
root = Column([h])
